Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:39:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: wacom_w9000: report a direct input device

The W9000-series digitizers sit under the display: a pen position is a
point on the screen, as with the other display digitizers (wacom_w8001,
the silead pen).  Without INPUT_PROP_DIRECT userspace takes the pen for
an external tablet: libinput does not bind it to a display, and Android
types a touch device without the property as a pointer.

Set INPUT_PROP_DIRECT.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820, W9019, firmware 0x0124): the
properties of the input device read 2 (INPUT_PROP_DIRECT) instead of 0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/wacom_w9000.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/wacom_w9000.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/wacom_w9000.c
index 008be43a13..d5f735976e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/wacom_w9000.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/wacom_w9000.c
@@ -488,6 +488,7 @@ static int wacom_w9000_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, BTN_TOOL_PEN);
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, BTN_TOOL_RUBBER);
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, BTN_STYLUS);
+	__set_bit(INPUT_PROP_DIRECT, input_dev->propbit);
 
 	input_set_abs_params(input_dev, ABS_X, 0, wacom_data->prop.max_x, 4, 0);
 	input_set_abs_params(input_dev, ABS_Y, 0, wacom_data->prop.max_y, 4, 0);
